  body: "# Qualifying year for State Pension in the DMG\n\n## Source-backed proposal\n\nThe chapter describes a
    qualifying year by reference to a tax year in working life and its earnings factor; it may consist entirely
    of credits. Pre-commencement and post-commencement years are distinguished.\n\n## Scope and exceptions\n\nA
    calendar year of employment is not automatically a qualifying year. This record does not verify a contribution
    record, award credits or calculate entitlement. The 6 April 2016 boundary, earlier reckonable years and relevant
    contribution rules remain part of the review.\n\n## Inspected passages\n\n- [DMG 74023, PDF page 4](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/69d8f255d3e08b8871b665ab/dmg-Ch-74.pdf#page=4).\n\
    - [DMG 74024, PDF page 4](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/69d8f255d3e08b8871b665ab/dmg-Ch-74.pdf#page=4).\n\
    - [DMG 74025, PDF page 5](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/69d8f255d3e08b8871b665ab/dmg-Ch-74.pdf#page=5).\n\
    - [DMG 74036, PDF page 6](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/69d8f255d3e08b8871b665ab/dmg-Ch-74.pdf#page=6).\n\
    \n## Provenance and review\n\nIndependent experimental interpretation of DWP guidance, not an official DWP document.
    All definitions and relationships are model-assisted and unreviewed. No individual eligibility, award, legal
    conclusion or executable rule is supplied.\n\nSource observation, listing-page update, printed revision, stated
    legal date and pension event date have separate meanings. PDF page numbers are one-based file positions; extraction
    may damage reading order, footnotes and characters. No visual PDF or specialist acceptance is claimed.\n\n-
    `dmg-vol12-ch74` — PDF SHA-256 `5961a9cb7c86814a0f6fa147c0a8a551b4258c803680fac14a95cab9eca1afd6`; page-extraction
    SHA-256 `c762e93940b4342d70d5bc96a80c3e094c91852d93868f5709e04f293faef61a`.\n"
  semantic_relations:
  - target: term/sp-transitional-rate
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: The transitional provision refers separately to qualifying years and pre-commencement
      qualifying years; the relation preserves that distinction.
    evidence:
    - page: page/dmg-vol12-ch74/0015
      quote: "74202 A person is entitled to SP payable at the transitional rate if they have\n\n\n1. reached pensionable
        age1 and\n\n\n2. at least 10 qualifying years2 and\n\n\n3. at least one pre-commencement qualifying year3.\n\
        \n\nNote 1: See DMG 74022 for the meaning of pensionable age, DMG 74023 for the meaning of qualifying\n\
        year and DMG 74024 for the meaning of pre-commencement qualifying year.\n\n\nNote 2: See DMG 74012 for guidance
        on references to HMRC if there is a dispute about a NI contribution\nrecord.\n\n\nNote 3: See DMG Chapter
        03 for guidance on revision where there is a late award of contributions or\ncredits, or because of changes
        to Class 2 NI collection."
      locator: DMG 74202
